1. PURPOSE

This Software License Agreement (“License”) governs the use of the Bulloch Transport software and related technology provided by TJ Studios LLC (“Licensor”) to Bulloch County Schools (“Licensee”).

The purpose of this License is to permit Licensee to use the software for authorized school transportation operations while establishing the ownership, use, modification, distribution, and maintenance rights associated with the software.

⸻

2. DEFINITIONS

2.1 “Software”

“Software” means the Bulloch Transport software developed, maintained, or provided by Licensor, including applicable:

* application software;
* Raspberry Pi software;
* device-management software;
* navigation software;
* user interfaces;
* APIs;
* backend services;
* administrative dashboards;
* update systems;
* deployment tools;
* scripts;
* configuration systems;
* documentation;
* custom graphics and interfaces;
* security components; and
* related software components created by Licensor.

2.2 “Authorized Device”

An “Authorized Device” means a Raspberry Pi, computer, server, touchscreen system, or other hardware specifically approved for use with Bulloch Transport.

2.3 “Update”

An “Update” means a software update, security patch, bug fix, feature update, configuration update, firmware update, dependency update, or other modification supplied by Licensor.

2.4 “School Data”

“School Data” means information supplied by or belonging to Licensee that is processed through the Software.

⸻

3. COPYRIGHT OWNERSHIP

Except for third-party software and materials, Licensor retains all right, title, and interest in the Software and its original components.

This includes applicable copyrights, source code, object code, software architecture, interfaces, documentation, designs, algorithms, deployment systems, and other original works.

Nothing in this License transfers ownership of the Software to Licensee.

⸻

4. LICENSE GRANT

Subject to the terms of this License, Licensor grants Licensee a:

non-exclusive, limited, non-transferable license

to install, execute, display, and use the Software on Authorized Devices for the internal transportation and operational purposes of Bulloch County Schools.

The license is limited to the authorized Bulloch Transport environment.

⸻

5. AUTHORIZED USE

Licensee may use the Software to:

* operate school transportation systems;
* operate authorized bus Devices;
* manage transportation routes;
* support authorized drivers;
* monitor authorized transportation operations;
* perform administrative transportation functions;
* perform authorized maintenance;
* access authorized dashboards;
* receive Software Updates; and
* use other features provided by the Software.

⸻

6. INSTALLATION

Licensee may install the Software on Authorized Devices designated for Bulloch Transport.

Licensee shall not intentionally install the Software on unauthorized systems or distribute installation packages to unauthorized parties.

⸻

7. SOFTWARE UPDATES

Licensee authorizes Licensor to provide Updates to Authorized Devices.

Updates may include:

* application updates;
* security patches;
* operating-system updates;
* dependency updates;
* firmware updates;
* configuration updates;
* performance improvements;
* bug fixes;
* navigation improvements;
* device-management improvements; and
* emergency security updates.

Updates may be delivered automatically or manually.

⸻

8. REMOTE ADMINISTRATION

As part of maintaining the Software, Licensee may authorize Licensor to remotely administer Authorized Devices.

Remote administration may use technologies including:

* Tailscale;
* SSH;
* authenticated management services;
* secure APIs;
* device-management agents; and
* other security-approved mechanisms.

Remote administration is limited to Authorized Devices and legitimate Software maintenance, security, troubleshooting, and support purposes.

Additional remote-access terms may be established in a separate Device Management & Remote Access Agreement.

⸻

9. MODIFICATION BY LICENSEE

Licensee may configure the Software using configuration options intentionally provided by Licensor.

Licensee may not modify proprietary portions of the Software unless expressly authorized in writing by Licensor.

Nothing in this section restricts rights that Licensee has under applicable law.

⸻

10. SOURCE CODE

Unless separately agreed in writing, this License does not grant Licensee ownership of or unrestricted access to the Software’s source code.

Providing source code for development, auditing, maintenance, security review, or another authorized purpose does not transfer copyright ownership.

⸻

11. REDISTRIBUTION

Licensee may not sell, sublicense, publish, redistribute, lease, rent, or otherwise provide the Software to an unauthorized third party.

Licensee may not create a separate commercial software product based substantially on the Software without a separate written agreement with Licensor.

⸻

12. REVERSE ENGINEERING

Licensee shall not reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or otherwise attempt to derive the source code or underlying structure of proprietary portions of the Software except to the extent such activity cannot legally be restricted under applicable law.

⸻

13. THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE

The Software may contain or interact with third-party software, open-source software, operating systems, libraries, APIs, or services.

Third-party components remain owned by their respective authors or licensors.

Those components are governed by their applicable licenses.

Where a third-party license grants rights that cannot be restricted by this License, those rights remain unaffected.

