14. SCHOOL DATA

Licensee retains ownership of its School Data.

Nothing in this License transfers ownership of School Data to Licensor.

Licensor may process or access School Data only as reasonably necessary to provide, maintain, secure, troubleshoot, update, or support the Software, subject to applicable law and any applicable data-protection agreement.

⸻

15. DATA SECURITY

Licensor shall use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards appropriate to the Software and its intended use.

Security measures may include:

* authentication;
* authorization;
* encryption;
* access controls;
* Tailscale network controls;
* SSH authentication;
* device identity;
* logging;
* credential management;
* security updates; and
* vulnerability remediation.

⸻

16. SECURITY UPDATES

Licensor may deploy emergency security Updates when reasonably necessary to address a significant vulnerability, active security threat, or critical system failure.

Emergency Updates may be deployed outside scheduled maintenance periods when reasonably necessary to protect Authorized Devices or the Software environment.

⸻

17. MAINTENANCE WINDOW

Routine Updates may be scheduled during an agreed maintenance window.

The intended maintenance window is:

9:00 PM Eastern Time

The maintenance window may be changed by mutual agreement.

Emergency security maintenance may occur outside the scheduled window when reasonably necessary.

⸻

18. AVAILABILITY

Licensor will make reasonable efforts to maintain the Software.

However, Licensee acknowledges that system availability may depend on:

* Internet connectivity;
* cellular connectivity;
* power;
* Raspberry Pi hardware;
* third-party services;
* cloud infrastructure;
* mapping services;
* weather services;
* authentication providers;
* network infrastructure; and
* other external systems.

Licensor does not guarantee uninterrupted operation of every component.

